        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "ad073272d7e528b2beecb0ec63c0bab0fb0d1785",
            "parents": [
                "80cde632088394b9b3da90cf677b8d2763278c77"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/57/87957/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "createdOn": 1773232505,
            "author": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm++/_abi_annotation.hpp",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "how do these macros normally get injected?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm++/_abi_annotation.hpp",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "In the C library they're injected into the implementation by the compiler rather than through the public headers:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/80cde632088394b9b3da90cf677b8d2763278c77/meson.build#L70\n\nIn light of the C++ support, maybe we should change that."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm++/_abi_annotation.hpp",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "ok, i can try to adjust it on the C side as well to put the macros on both the declaration and the definition.\n\nAs a result of that change some things can come out of `config.h.in` and go into a header `_abi_annotation.h` which can then has to included by all libpldm and libpldm++ headers and implementation files.\n\nForgetting to include that header in some other header would then cause a build failure for library users which is a tradeoff, in the existing implementation there is no need to be careful there since the ABI macros are provided by `config.h`.\n\nAlso there would be a problem since a mismatch between header and source is possible.\n\nI explored this possible rework in https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/88254"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm++/_abi_annotation.hpp",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Based on the discussion in 88254, changed it to match the existing usage of ABI annotation in libpldm. It looks like that's well tested and supported in gcc."
                }
            ],
